@startuml MonitoringTool-DataFlow
title MATISSE IFARLAB-EDIH Monitoring Tool -- Live Telemetry & Manual Control Flow

actor User
participant "Browser\n(client, React + Three.js)" as Browser
participant "api/server.js\n(Express + SSE)" as API
database "MongoDB Atlas\n(joint_states collection)" as Mongo

== Startup ==
User -> Browser : open app
Browser -> API : GET /api/telemetry/joint-states/stream\n(new EventSource)
activate API
API --> Browser : event: hello
API -> Mongo : ensureConnected()
activate Mongo
Mongo --> API : connection OK
deactivate Mongo

== Live telemetry (every request-interval, min 250ms) ==
loop until the browser tab closes the connection
  API -> Mongo : findOne({_id: "latest"})\n(fallback: sort by ts desc)
  activate Mongo
  Mongo --> API : { ts, ur10e[7 rad], kawasaki[7 rad] }
  deactivate Mongo
  API -> API : toArmDegrees() -- indices 1-6, rad -> deg\ntoRailPosition() -- index 0, metres passthrough
  API --> Browser : event: joint_states\n{ ur10e[6], ur10eRail, kawasaki[6], agvRail, timestamp }
  Browser -> Browser : setJointAngles / setKawasakiAngles\nsetRailPosition / setAgvRailPosition
  Browser -> Browser : Three.js re-renders both robots\nat the new joint pose
end

== Manual control (any time) ==
User -> Browser : drag a joint / rail / gripper slider
Browser -> Browser : setState directly (no network call)
Browser -> Browser : Three.js re-renders immediately
note right of Browser
  Incoming live "joint_states" events are ignored
  while "Play demo animation" is on, so live and
  manual control never fight outside of that case.
end note

== Demo animation (optional) ==
Browser -> Browser : RailAnimator + per-robot useFrame hooks\nmutate Three.js refs directly every frame\n(bypasses React state for smooth 60fps motion)

deactivate API
@enduml
